      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Prioritizing political messaging over aesthetic beauty has created a bifurcated market where \"activist art\" often commands higher prices due to its perceived urgency, while traditional craft-focused works are increasingly undervalued by collectors seeking social relevance. This shift is not a failure of art but a necessary evolution that forces artists to confront uncomfortable truths, even if it sometimes sacrifices technical refinement for raw emotional impact. The value of contemporary art is now inextricably linked to its ability to challenge power structures, making the most politically potent pieces the most commercially successful, regardless of their aesthetic purity.",
